## Third-party notices

This package contains code derived from pi, distributed under the MIT License:

  pi — https://github.com/earendil-works/pi
  Copyright (c) Mario Zechner
  Licensed under the MIT License
  Affected packages: @earendil-works/pi-tui,
                     @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent

The pi components under `src/tui/` are transcribed rather than vendored: the
behaviour is ported and the dependency is not (see `src/tui/message-view.ts` for
the reasoning). The files concerned are the ones whose header says so —
"transcribed from pi's own implementations", "transcribed from pi's", or "pi's
shape". Files that merely mention pi without such a note describe pi's behaviour
in prose and contain no ported code.

pi is distributed under the MIT License, which requires its copyright notice and
permission notice to accompany copies of the software. The copyright notice is
stated above; the permission notice is the MIT text at the top of this file —
the same terms, applied to this package's own copyright line as well.
